{number: 155}
{title: I’ll Fly Away}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
Some glad morning when this life is o’er,
I’ll fly away
To a home on God’s celestial shore,
I’ll fly away
I’ll fly away
I’ll fly away
When I die, hallelujah, by and by,
I’ll fly away
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
When the shadows of this life have gone,
I’ll fly away
Like a bird from prison bars has flown
I’ll fly away
I’ll fly away
I’ll fly away
When I die, hallelujah, by and by,
I’ll fly away
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Just a few more weary days and then,
I’ll fly away
To a land where joys shall never end,
I’ll fly away
I’ll fly away
I’ll fly away
When I die, hallelujah, by and by,
I’ll fly away
{end_of_verse}
